$MDESC::Creator = "Capture the Flag";
$MDESC::Type = "CTF Mixed";
$MDESC::Text = "<s3><f1>Mission Type: <f0> VIP Assassination" @
         "\n<f1>Planet: <f0> Azalcar" @
         "\n<f1>Weather: <f0> Cloudy, Misty and Cool" @
         "\n<f1>Time of Day: <f0> Early Morning" @ 
         "\n<f1># of Teams: <f0> 2" @
         "\n\n<f1>Briefing:<f0> The world of Azalcar is devoid of plentiful water resources.  Due to the extreme heat suffered here for most of the year the water reserves of the planet vaporize and remain airborn locked away from the parched land below.  Once a year, however, a great torrential downpour causes great floods to course over the desert world's barren flood plains.  Not only can this water be captured and stored for later use, but it can also be used to generate a great deal of hydroelectric power.  Owners of the massive dams of this world can make a killing selling water and power, two commodities that are never in enough supply.\n\nIt is one month before the great annual flooding is to occur and the <$server::teamname1> team was preparing their dam for the coming season when disaster struck.  The <$server::teamname0> team has filed a completely spurious complaint about a lack of safety in the dam's operation in hopes that the government of Alzalcar, not willing to let any drop of water go unharvested, will declare the dam's current operators incompetent and give the dam to them instead.  To make matters worse, the Inspector assigned to inspect the dam's facilities is widely known to be under <$server::teamname0> pay.  The <$server::teamname1> team will not give up without a fight though, they have acquired a clever, master of disguise to take on the identity of the Inspector and impersonate him, ensuring that they will receive a favorable report.  The only trick now is to kill the rival Inspector...\n\nKill the enemy Inspector while defending your own.  The first team to assassinate the enemy Inspector shall be declared the victor!";
